     }

     private connection(): void {}
   }
   ```

   This code sets up the basic structure of an Express server by creating a constructor and methods for configuration, routing, and database connection (which is not implemented in this example).

   To add your own middleware, simply import your middleware and add it to the `config()` method.

   To add more routes, simply add new middleware functions to the `routes()` method:

   ```typescript
